- `@.cursor/rules/ui-components.mdc` - UI component standards
- `@.cursor/rules/testing.mdc` - Testing patterns and practices

## Rule Precedence

When multiple rules apply, they are merged in this order:

1. **Team Rules** (if on Team/Enterprise plan)
2. **Project Rules** (`.cursor/rules/`)
3. **User Rules** (global preferences)

Earlier sources take precedence when guidance conflicts.

## Common Patterns

### Rule for Specific File Types

```md
---
globs: server/**/*.ts
description: Server-side TypeScript guidelines
alwaysApply: false
---
```

### Always-Applied Rule

```md
---
description: Project-wide coding standards
alwaysApply: true
---
```

### Manual-Only Rule (Template)

```md
---
description: API endpoint template
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

Use this template when creating API endpoints:
@api-template.ts
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

❌ **Don't**: Create one massive rule covering everything
✅ **Do**: Split into focused, composable rules

❌ **Don't**: Write vague, abstract guidance
✅ **Do**: Provide concrete examples and clear instructions

❌ **Don't**: Create rules that duplicate existing documentation
✅ **Do**: Reference official docs and add project-specific context

❌ **Don't**: Create rules longer than 500 lines
✅ **Do**: Split large rules into multiple files

